      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never storing it there in the first place.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of the spawned child process** (the Ingest agent) immediately before that process starts.\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** with the credential.\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the API key simply by having someone inspect its environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model applies to the Query agent process as well: it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
      "input_tokens": 5280,
      "output_tokens": 222
    }
